 "text": "Hey, nice have a supportive friend by your side. Listen to the thunder as it gets farther away, and keep an eye on the sky. If the sky turns dark and it starts pouring, find dry spot inside and cover up. Stick to a well cleared path and take breaks if you need to. Thunderstorms don't usually last long. Of course. Pack up as you leave, so the tent is ready the next day. Pack up as you leave, so the tent is ready the next day. Find a building and see if you can stay there overnight. Jump off only if the electrical system is turned off and there' no rain for several hours. Stick to the path and find dry spot. Get everyone inside as soon as it starts pouring.",
